cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Modrag-dock: a conversational agent for protein-ligand docking"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it along with the docking methods it
  builds on (listed under references).
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Cafiero
    given-names: Mauricio
repository-code: "https://github.com/MauricioCafiero/dock_assist"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A command-line agent that drives protein-ligand docking from natural
  language: it searches the PDB, retrieves receptors, resolves ligand SMILES,
  and docks with AutoDock Vina. Binding sites can be found by a pure-Python
  buriedness grid scan, taken from a co-crystallized ligand centroid, or
  specified directly. Metal sites are docked with the AutoDock4Zn force field
  for zinc and tiered AutoGrid parameter sets for eleven other metals.
  Covalent inhibitors are docked with the AutoDock flexible-side-chain
  covalent protocol, with the warhead reacted onto the target cysteine or
  serine from the free drug SMILES.
keywords:
  - molecular docking
  - drug discovery
  - AutoDock Vina
  - covalent docking
  - metalloprotein
  - large language model agent

